  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1007 PM CDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\nA brief respite from the extreme heat is expected Tuesday as a\nfront settles south and NW flow increases aloft. Highs should\nsettle into the low to mid 90s, closer to seasonal normals, with\nlower humidity and mostly sunny skies. Overnight lows drop into\nthe upper 60s to low 70s. \n\nBy Wednesday and Thursday, southerly return flow may allow\ntemperatures to rebound somewhat into the mid to upper 90s, though\nheat indices are not expected to reach as high as the previous\nweekend. Isolated afternoon showers or storms remain possible but\ncoverage looks limited. \n\nToward the end of the next week into next weekend, global models\nshow better agreement on a broader trough amplifying over the\neastern U.S. This evolution should finally push he ridge farther \nSW and open the door for more widespread rain chances and a return\nto near normal or slightly below normal temperatures by next \nSunday. Confidence increases in the overall cooling trend but \nremains moderate on exact precipitation timing and amounts through\nthe second half of next week.",
